# FOCUS-TIER repos — standalone products you are driving to market.
# These sit JUST BELOW the core priority repos (config/schedule_priority.txt)
# and ABOVE all other repos.
#
# Effect (enforced by scripts/reprioritize_queue.sh):
#   • CORE repos (schedule_priority.txt) — untouched (keep P0/P1).
#   • FOCUS repos (this file) — any task better than P2 is capped to P2 (so the
#     core P0/P1 always drains first, but these focus apps still outrank the rest).
#   • EVERY OTHER repo — capped to P3 (bottom).
#
# One repo name per line (task-store convention = git basename). '#' lines ignored.
#
# Example:
#   side-project-one
#   side-project-two
#
# This .example file is the fork-ready template. Copy to `schedule_focus.txt`
# and list your focus-tier repo basenames.
